## Phase 4: Importing S3 and resolving tag drifts

Next, I added `aws_s3_bucket.own_mport_s3` to `resou.tf` and imported my existing S3 bucket via CLI:

```bash
terraform import aws_s3_bucket.own_mport_s3 my-car-bucket-2645

```

Once imported, I ran `terraform plan`. It detected tag drifts:

* The real EC2 instance on AWS had a tag `"Name" = "my-car-ec2"`, but my local `resou.tf` code did not include it. Terraform planned to drop it (`- "Name" = "my-car-ec2" -> null`).
* My local code for `aws_s3_bucket` specified two new tags (`Managedby = "Terra_car"` and `lifecycle = "Critical_factor"`). Terraform planned to add them to AWS.

```text
Plan: 0 to add, 2 to change, 0 to destroy.

```

I ran `terraform apply --auto-approve` to update both real AWS resources so they fully aligned with my code.

